Q: What does &quot;Not a HASH reference&quot; mean? A: <p>You can dereference the array with <code>@{}</code>.  I see no need to use <a href="https://perldoc.perl.org/functions/values" rel="noreferrer">values</a> here:</p>
<pre><code>my @IDs = @{ $Body-&gt;{'ConfigItemSearchResponse'}-&gt;{'ConfigItemIDs'} };
</code></pre>

Q: Hide HTML blocks with their respective button A: <p>Navigate to the adjacent block by using <code>nextElementSibling</code>, and attach the event listeners properly by using <code>addEventListener</code> instead:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>for (const button of document.querySelectorAll('button')) {
  button.addEventListener('click', () =&gt; {
    button.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('hidden');
  });
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>button {
  display: block;
}
.hidden {
  display: none;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="main"&gt;
  &lt;button&gt;Hide Block 1&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;block 1&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;button&gt;Hide Block 2&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;block 2&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How do jQuery animations start from the end? A: <pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;box&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>When the menu is closed, it adds display: none property to the .box element. You have to add this style property to the .box element in HTML to make it look trapped on boot.</p>
